This is **this repository's** bug ledger: one dated line per mistake already paid for
here. `pitfalls.md` next to it holds the rules that are true of any NestJS Clean
Architecture service; this file holds the ones that are only true here.

The skill reads both before finishing any change. A change that reintroduces a line from
this file is not done.

## How it grows

Add a line when:

- a bug reached the branch and had to be fixed — the line is the rule that would have
  prevented it;
- the user corrected the same thing twice — the second time it becomes a line here
  instead of a third correction;
- a decision was taken because of something that went wrong (not a design preference —
  those belong in the project's decision log).

Do **not** add: style opinions, restatements of the universal `pitfalls.md`, or anything
that is already enforced by a type, a lint rule or a test. If a rule can be made
executable, make it executable and do not write it here.

Keep the file as a flat, dated list. It is read top to bottom, so when it passes roughly
forty lines, delete what a type or a test now enforces rather than adding sections.

## Format

One line per entry:

```
YYYY-MM-DD — <the rule, in the imperative> — <why: what broke> — <where: file or module>
```

Example:

```
2026-09-15 — The round word never appears in a payload before `round:end` — a debug
field on the guess ack shipped the answer to every client — `gateway/presentation/`,
`rooms/domain/services/state-presenter.ts`
```

